Severs the only channel by which the STOMP benchmark harness sees a
collision, for the mutation arm of the STOMP condition-2 measurement.

get_collision_cost_function returns collision_penalty when
PlanningScene::is_state_colliding fires and 0.0 otherwise, and
cost_function_from_state_validator lowers validity only when a
waypoint's cost exceeds 0.0. With the penalty itself at 0.0 no waypoint
can read invalid, so STOMP has no collision gradient to descend.

Base commit: ad3a1e01. Applying this with git apply and running
  cargo build --release -p cspace-planners --example stomp_benchmark_port
reproduces the mutated binary this measurement used, byte for byte;
reverting reproduces the unmutated one, also byte for byte. Both
equalities were checked with cmp when the patch was written.

